BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20270126T230000Z
DTEND:20270127T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20270126T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mental Health Support Group (NAMI's Connection Recovery Peer Support Group)
DESCRIPTION: \n\nThe Essex-Passaic Chapter of NAMI (The National Alliance 
 on Mental Illness) Connection Recovery Peer Support Group Program meets on 
 the 4th Tuesday of each month at the West Caldwell Library on 30 Clinton 
 Road. \n\nNAMI is the most influential organization devoted to helping 
 people with mental illness and their relatives and loved ones recover and 
 deal with mental health issues. These meetings will be led by people having 
 some form of mental illness. During these meetings\, we will conduct peer 
 support though all people interested in this organization are encouraged to 
 attend. You do not have to sign up in advance. All meetings are kept 
 confidential and are led by people specifically trained to conduct these 
 meetings.\n\n NAMI Connection is a recovery peer support group program that 
 offers respect\, understanding\, encouragement and hope. NAMI Connection 
 groups are:\n\n·       Free and confidential\n\n·       Held monthly for 
 90 minutes  \n\n·       Designed to connect\, encourage\, and support 
 participants using a structured support group model\n\n·       Led by 
 trained facilitators living in recovery themselves\n\nThis meeting is for 
 anyone ages 18  who is dealing with their own mental illness or a loved 
 one's.  \n\n \n\nhttps://nami.org/Home
LOCATION:West Caldwell - Community Meeting Room
ORGANIZER;CN="West Caldwell Public Library":MAILTO:programs@westcaldwell.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
UID:LibCal-10340-16961906
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16961906
END:VEVENT
